From 818cfdb15fc60411b3e2a7fa37582829e03f15fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:16:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64_ilp32: use the aarch64 math functions

The aarch64 math sources are inline asm on floating point registers and
work unchanged for ILP32. Without them the generic C fma and fmaf failed
libc-test. lrint, lrintf, lround and lroundf are left out: they convert
into a 64-bit register, which for a 32-bit long truncates instead of
raising FE_INVALID, so the generic versions are used.
